While twm is very lite I wouldn't recomend it for anyone who isn't
very knowledgable about *nix.  When I came back to X I started on twm
and worked with it for 6 months.  The only way to make it usable was
to be very versed in creating shell scripts to launch from the menuing
system.  After a while having to manually place windows got annoying
and I moved up to blackbox.  Blackbox is maybe 4 times as large as twm
but much eaiser to work with.  After development stalled on that I
moved up to fluxbox.  It is about 10 times the size of twm but worth
the extra 900K.  Xfce offers a lot more but at 20M in size it is 1% of
his total disk space instead of .005% of his disk space.  As it is he
is going to want almost 1/8th of his drive space for swap.  Though I
